      "text": "VALENTIN FÉRAY AND PIOTR ŚNIADY Tr ρλ(π) a max Tr ρλ(e) — We prove an upper bound for characters of the symmetric groups.\n\n**VALENTIN FÉRAY AND PIOTR ŚNIADY Tr ρλ(π) a max Tr ρλ(e)**\n\n20 pp, 26 sections.\n\n**Abstract.** We prove an upper bound for characters of the symmetric groups. Namely, we show that there exists a constant a > 0 with a property that for every Young diagram λ with n boxes, r(λ) rows and c(λ) columns \u0013\u0015|π| \u0012r(λ) n , |π| n , c(λ) , n where |π| is the minimal number of factors needed to write π ∈Sn as a product of transpositions. We also give uniform estimates for the error term in the Vershik-Kerov’s and Biane’s character formulas and give a new formula for free cumulants of the transition measure. 1.1. Normalized characters. For a Young diagram λ having n boxes and a permutation π ∈Sl (where l ≤n) we deﬁne the normalized character where (n)l = n(n −1) · · ·(n −l + 1) denotes the falling power and where Tr ρλ(e) 1.2. Short history of the problem.\n\n**Outline.** Front matter; 1 Introduction; 1.1 Normalized characters; 1.2 Short history of the problem; 1.3 The main result; 1.4 Young diagrams; 1.5 The main tool: reformulation of Stanley ch; 1.6 Overview of the paper; 2 Stanley character formula; 2.1 Young symmetrizer; 2.2 Forgetting injectivity; 2.3 Generalization to Young diagrams on R+2; 3 Characters of symmetric groups, random matri; 3.1 Stanley character formula and random matri; 3.2 Free cumulants of the transition measure; 3.3 Generalized circular operators; 4 Technical estimates; 4.1 Estimates for the number of colorings N(1,",
